\ port/lab/host.4 - what relfsh needs of a forth-vm-evolution design beyond
\ port/os.4: the design's kernel is relf's of long ago (the lab forked it),
\ so most of the shell's words are there under relf's names - START, S0, R0,
\ SRC, SID, TIB, the search order's cells - and SYSCALL is its engine's.

BASE @  DECIMAL

2 ARG-BASE !                       \ argv: the engine, the image, then the shell's own
-1 ALLOCATE-ZEROES !               \ a design's ALLOCATE is an anonymous mmap
\ DICT-LIMIT is relf's address where the dictionary must stop, the stacks
\ being above it; the shell's only use is its guard for the forth
\ command's 16 KB gap (STACK-GAP-ROOM), which reports an overflow when the
\ gap would end within 8 KB of it. A design keeps its stacks in a chunk of
\ their own (STACKSEP), 256 KB of data stack under a guard page, so here
\ it is that floor less those 8 KB, from the stack pointer at boot.
262144 CONSTANT DSTACK-BYTES        \ every design's DSTACK_BYTES
VARIABLE DSTACK-TOP   0 DSTACK-TOP !
: DICT-LIMIT ( --- a-addr )  DSTACK-TOP @ DSTACK-BYTES - 4096 + 1024 +  8192 - ;

\ ---- extend.4's search order, on the design's word list ---------------
\ The design's word list is relf's of before the link cell: [count][heads],
\ the wid being the count's address, the heads absolute (COLD relocates
\ FORTH-WORDLIST's), the links in the chain relative. WORDLIST lays relf's
\ link cell in front again, a START-relative offset of the previous one,
\ so save.4 can find each word list made before the image is saved and
\ make its heads relative, and PORT-BOOT absolute again; COLD knows only
\ FORTH-WORDLIST. The rest is extend.4's.
: .( ( "ccc<rparen>" --- )  41 PARSE TYPE ; IMMEDIATE
: GET-ORDER ( --- w1 w2 ... wn n )
  #ORDER @ 0 ?DO CONTEXT I CELLS + @ LOOP #ORDER @ ;
: SET-ORDER ( w1 w2 ... wn n --- )
  #ORDER ! 0 #ORDER @ 1- DO CONTEXT I CELLS + ! -1 +LOOP ;
: ALSO ( --- )  CONTEXT #ORDER @ CELLS + DUP 1 CELLS - @ SWAP ! 1 #ORDER +! ;
: PREVIOUS ( --- )  -1 #ORDER +! ;
: WORDLIST ( --- wid )
  ALIGN WORDLISTS @ ,
  HERE DUP START @ - WORDLISTS !
  FORTH-WORDLIST @ ,
  HERE FORTH-WORDLIST @ CELLS DUP ALLOT 0 FILL ;
: DEFINITIONS ( --- )  CONTEXT #ORDER @ 1- CELLS + @ CURRENT ! ;
: FORTH ( --- )  FORTH-WORDLIST CONTEXT #ORDER @ 1- CELLS + ! ;
WORDLIST START @ -  CONSTANT ROOT-WORDLIST-OFFSET
: ROOT-WORDLIST ( --- wid )   ROOT-WORDLIST-OFFSET START @ + ;
: ONLY ( --- )  1 #ORDER ! ROOT-WORDLIST CONTEXT ! ;
: VOCABULARY ( --- )
  WORDLIST START @ - CREATE  ,
  DOES> >R
  GET-ORDER SWAP DROP R> @ START @ + SWAP SET-ORDER ;
VARIABLE WL-XT
: WORDLISTS-DO ( xt --- )   \ xt ( a-addr --- ) on each nonzero head of each
  WL-XT !  WORDLISTS @
  BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    START @ +                                     ( wid )
    DUP @ 1+ 1 DO
      DUP I CELLS + DUP @ IF WL-XT @ EXECUTE ELSE DROP THEN
    LOOP
    1 CELLS - @
  REPEAT ;
ROOT-WORDLIST CURRENT !
: FORTH FORTH ;
: ALSO ALSO ;
: ONLY ONLY ;
: PREVIOUS PREVIOUS ;
: DEFINITIONS DEFINITIONS ;
DEFINITIONS

BASE !
